.TH qsh-service-uninstall 1  "uninstall 0.5.8" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-service\-uninstall \- Remove the unit for this machine\*(Aqs inferred run mode, if any. Without `\-\-deactivate` a running unit stays running
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh service uninstall\fR [\fB\-\-deactivate\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-always\-on\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-ssh\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove the unit for this machine\*(Aqs inferred run mode, if any. Without `\-\-deactivate` a running unit stays running
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-deactivate\fR
Release the unit from the service manager first (`launchctl bootout` / `systemctl \-\-user disable \-\-now` / `schtasks /End` then `/Delete`), then remove the unit file. The file is kept if the release fails
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-always\-on\fR
Reverse `install \-\-always\-on`: `loginctl disable\-linger` (Linux), the LaunchDaemon removed under `sudo` (macOS), or the `Password` task and the firewall rule deleted from an elevated console (Windows)
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-ssh\fR
Never run ssh on this command\*(Aqs behalf: no automatic bootstrap of an unknown name, and no restarting of a pinned host\*(Aqs serve over ssh when the connection fails (`docs/CLI.md` §7). `qsh pair ssh` is not affected; it is ssh by definition
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH VERSION
v0.5.8
